          "Their mother helps them look around the flat. She checks the hall and the kitchen, while Elif looks under her bed. Can suddenly remembers that he carried the bag to the car after last week’s practice. Their father hardly ever uses the car on weekdays, so the bag is still in the boot. Elif finds it and thanks him for remembering.",
          "After that, Elif makes a small checklist. She always checks the car first, then the hall, and finally her bedroom. She also writes her name on the towel because Can often thinks it is his. The new routine is simple, but it helps her feel calm before practice."
